  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Assistance to Victims of Trafficking, Exploitation and Abuse Identified in Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the support of the UK Foreign, Commonwealth &amp; Development Office (FCDO), the International Organization for Migration (IOM) aims to contribute to reducing the vulnerabilities of Victims of Trafficking in Libya, especially women and children. In pursuit of this objective, IOM will implement two main activities which aim to provide victims of trafficking, exploitation and abuse access to life-saving protection services and assistance in Libya and in their countries of origin. The first will entail conducting Protection Case Management Assessments to identify vulnerable migrants and providing tailored assistance. The second activity will involve providing individual reintegration assistance to victims of trafficking, exploitation and abuse in their countries of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
